    "body": "The owner asked for a review brief so that a fresh session, with no memory of the runs, can evaluate the process that moves the platform forward. It covers:\n\n- flaws;\n- improvements;\n- tools, judged against best practice;\n- new projects;\n- changes to project priority.\n\nThis PR adds the brief. It changes no process.\n\n- `docs/research/2026-09-26-process-review/BRIEF.md` has nine sections:\n  - the flow stage by stage, with **what enforces each step: a machine, or only a brief**;\n  - eight days of runs, and the measured evidence (at `origin/main` `60878a9`);\n  - the review's questions and method, plus the coordinator's own suspicions, to be read after the reviewer's first pass;\n  - hard constraints: read-only on the process, one report PR, no issues filed, and a budget;\n  - the shape of `REPORT.md`, a reading map, and the launch line.\n- `evidence/measure-flow.mjs` re-measures every GitHub number the brief cites; its output is `evidence/2026-09-26-measurements.txt`.\n- `README.md` indexes the directory; `REPORT.md` will be written by the reviewing session.\n\nFive draft claims failed a check against their sources while this was written, and were corrected before commit (brief §5, method 4). The brief tells the reviewer to expect more.\n\nDecisions: none\n\n**Verification**\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `pnpm run lint:docs` | exit 0 |\n| `eslint` on the evidence script | exit 0 |\n| pre-commit (`tsc -b`, doc paths) | passed |\n| `evidence/measure-flow.mjs` | exit 0 |\n| Leak scan (absolute paths, account ids) | clean |\n\nDocs-only. The size is 384 reviewable lines; `evidence/` is excluded."
